/-!
# The completion functor over a complete local ring along a principal ideal

Fix the standing situation of [Stacks, Tag 0EHC]: a Noetherian ring `A` with ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞`, the
affine scheme `X = Spec(A)`, its closed subschemes `Y = V(I)` and `Z = V(𝔞)`, and the open
complement `U = X ∖ Z`. [Stacks, Tag 0EKY] assumes

1. `A` has a dualizing complex and is `I`-adically complete,
2. `I = (f)` is generated by a single element,
3. `A` is local with maximal ideal `𝔞 = 𝔪`,
4. one of the following is true:
   * (a) `A_f` is `(S₂)` and `dim(A/𝔭) ≥ 4` for every minimal prime `𝔭` of `A` with `f ∉ 𝔭`, or
   * (b) `depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 3` for every prime `𝔭 ∉ V(f)` with `V(𝔭) ∩ V(f) ≠ {𝔪}`,

and concludes that, writing `U₀ = U ∩ V(f)`, the completion functor

  `colim_{U₀ ⊆ U' ⊆ U} Coh(𝒪_{U'}) ⟶ Coh(U, f𝒪_U)`

is an equivalence on the full subcategories of finite locally free objects.

## The source's proof

* Full faithfulness is [Stacks, Tag 0EKU]. Its hypothesis asks, for every associated prime `𝔭`
  of `A` off `V(f)` whose closure meets `V(f)` outside `{𝔪}`, that `dim(A/𝔭) > cd(A, (f)) + 1`.
  Since `cd(A, (f)) ≤ 1` it suffices that `dim(A/𝔭) ≥ 3`. An associated prime has
  `depth(A_𝔭) = 0`, so under (b) `dim(A/𝔭) > 3`; under (a) the Serre condition `(S₂)` at `A_𝔭`
  gives `min(2, dim A_𝔭) ≤ depth(A_𝔭) = 0`, so `𝔭` is minimal and `dim(A/𝔭) ≥ 4`.
* Essential surjectivity is [Stacks, Tag 0EJ9] (or [Stacks, Tag 0EJJ]). Its input is that a
  finite locally free object `(ℱₙ)` satisfies the `(2, 3)`-inequalities, which is
  [Stacks, Tag 0EJB]: the completed stalks `ℱ_y^∧` at `y ∈ U₀` are finite free over the completed
  local rings, so they are free at every prime off `V(f)`. This gives a coherent `𝒪_U`-module
  `ℱ` with completion `(ℱₙ)`. At `y ∈ U₀` the quotients `ℱ_y / fⁿ⁺¹ℱ_y` are the stalks of the
  `ℱₙ`, so they are finite free. A finite module over a Noetherian local ring is then free
  (`Stacks.FreeOfAdicQuotients.free_of_forall_free_quotient_pow_smul_top`). So `ℱ` is finite
  locally free on an open neighbourhood of `U₀`. Here `f` need not be a nonzerodivisor, unlike
  in [Stacks, Tag 0EKZ].

[Stacks, Tag 0EJB] asks `cd(A, I) = 1`. A principal ideal has `cd(A, (f)) ≤ 1`. If
`cd(A, (f)) ≤ 0`, then `(f)` is nilpotent in the local ring `A`, and every object of
`Coh(U, f𝒪_U)` extends to `X` without the inequalities
(`Stacks.Algebraization.extendsToX_of_pow_eq_bot`). This is the case split of the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0EJ9] in this library.

## Implementation notes

The dualizing complex of hypothesis (1) is asked for in an arbitrary model
`[HasDerivedCategory (ModuleCat A)]` of the derived category. The cited results
[Stacks, Tag 0EKU], [Stacks, Tag 0EJ9] and [Stacks, Tag 0EJB] are stated at
`HasDerivedCategory.standard`. The hypothesis is moved there by
`Dualizing.exists_isDualizingComplex_iff_of_models`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.free_completedStalk_of_hasFiniteFreeStalks`: the completed stalk of an
  object with finite free stalks is free at every point of `U₀`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.free_stalk_of_hasFiniteFreeStalks_completion_of_germ_mem_maximalIdeal`:
  a coherent module whose completion has finite free stalks is free at every point where the
  germ of `f` is not a unit, for any `f` with `I = (f)`.
* `isCompletionNearClosedFiniteLocallyFree_of_isLocalRing_of_eq_span_singleton`: the
  essential-surjectivity half of [Stacks, Tag 0EKY].
* `completionFullyFaithful_finiteLocallyFree_of_isLocalRing_of_eq_span_singleton`:
  the full-faithfulness half of [Stacks, Tag 0EKY].
* `Stacks.Algebraization.completionEquivalence_local_principal_finiteLocallyFree`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0EKY]**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EJ9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EJ9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EJB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EJB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHC)
-/

